Subject: [PATCH] session-lock: configure the lock surface when the monitor is turned

Against Hyprland v0.57.0 (src/protocols/SessionLock.cpp, SessionLock.hpp).

A lock surface gets its size in ext_session_lock_surface_v1.configure, and
CSessionLockSurface sends one whenever its monitor emits modeChanged. Since
the monitor rules are split into hard and soft properties, a rule change
that only differs in the transform is applied by
CMonitor::applyMonitorRuleSoft(): it gives the monitor its turned size, the
layout is arranged again (layer surfaces are configured, xdg_output sends
the new logical size), but modeChanged is not emitted. So a lock surface is
never told about a quarter turn: the client keeps drawing at the size the
surface was made with, and the renderer draws that buffer stretched over
the turned output until the session is unlocked. Touch no longer lines up
with what is drawn either.

Seen on a phone whose screen follows the accelerometer: locked on its side,
the screen is turned back to portrait a moment after the lock surface is
made, and the lock screen stays squeezed. With WAYLAND_DEBUG on a lock
client (1080x2424 at scale 8/3): ext_session_lock_surface_v1.configure(405,
909) at the lock, then none for four quarter turns, while
zxdg_output_v1.logical_size went to 909x405 and back each time.

Have the lock surface follow the monitor layout as well, as xdg_output
does, and send a configure when the monitor's size is no longer the one it
last sent.

diff --git i/src/protocols/SessionLock.cpp w/src/protocols/SessionLock.cpp
--- i/src/protocols/SessionLock.cpp
+++ w/src/protocols/SessionLock.cpp
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include "../output/Monitor.hpp"
 #include "../render/Renderer.hpp"
 #include "../desktop/state/FocusState.hpp"
+#include "../event/EventBus.hpp"
 
 CSessionLockSurface::CSessionLockSurface(SP<CExtSessionLockSurfaceV1> resource_, SP<CWLSurfaceResource> surface_, PHLMONITOR pMonitor_, WP<CSessionLock> owner_) :
     m_resource(resource_), m_sessionLock(owner_), m_surface(surface_), m_monitor(pMonitor_) {
@@ -68,6 +69,15 @@
             m_surface->enter(m_monitor.lock());
 
         m_listeners.monitorMode = m_monitor->m_events.modeChanged.listen([this] { sendConfigure(); });
+
+        // A rule change that only turns the monitor goes through applyMonitorRuleSoft(),
+        // which gives it its new size without modeChanged. Follow the layout as well, or
+        // the lock surface keeps the size it was made with and is drawn stretched over
+        // the turned output until the session is unlocked.
+        m_listeners.monitorLayout = Event::bus()->m_events.monitor.layoutChanged.listen([this] {
+            if (m_monitor && m_monitor->m_size != m_configuredSize)
+                sendConfigure();
+        });
     }
 
     sendConfigure();
@@ -88,6 +98,7 @@
     }
 
     const auto SERIAL = g_pSeatManager->nextSerial(g_pSeatManager->seatResourceForClient(m_resource->client()));
+    m_configuredSize  = m_monitor->m_size;
     m_resource->sendConfigure(SERIAL, m_monitor->m_size.x, m_monitor->m_size.y);
 }
 
diff --git i/src/protocols/SessionLock.hpp w/src/protocols/SessionLock.hpp
--- i/src/protocols/SessionLock.hpp
+++ w/src/protocols/SessionLock.hpp
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #include "WaylandProtocol.hpp"
 #include "ext-session-lock-v1.hpp"
 #include "../helpers/signal/Signal.hpp"
+#include "../helpers/math/Math.hpp"
 
 class CSessionLock;
 class CWLSurfaceResource;
@@ -33,11 +34,13 @@
 
     bool                         m_ackdConfigure = false;
     bool                         m_committed     = false;
+    Vector2D                     m_configuredSize;
 
     void                         sendConfigure();
 
     struct {
         CHyprSignalListener monitorMode;
+        CHyprSignalListener monitorLayout;
         CHyprSignalListener surfaceCommit;
         CHyprSignalListener surfaceDestroy;
     } m_listeners;
